TUnit uses `[Before(…)]` and `[After(…)]` attributes on **hook methods** (which must be `static` and return `Task`). The scope is set via the generic parameter or attribute argument.

---

### 1. Before/After every test in a class

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public static async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs before each [Test] in this class
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public static async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs after each [Test]
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task OrderIsCreated() { /* … */ }
}
```

---

### 2. Once before/after all tests in a class (class-scoped fixture)

```csharp
public class IntegrationTests
{
    private static ServiceFixture _fixture = null!;

    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _fixture = new ServiceFixture();
        await _fixture.InitializeAsync();
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        await _fixture.DisposeAsync();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task HealthCheckReturns200() { /* use _fixture */ }
}
```

---

### 3. Once before/after all tests in the assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockHook
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StartAsync();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StopAsync();
    }
}
```

The class can live anywhere in the assembly — TUnit discovers it automatically.

---

### 4. Once for the entire test session (global / test-run scope)

```csharp
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

This runs once across all assemblies in the test run.

---

### Quick reference

| Scope | Attribute | Context parameter | Runs… |
|-------|-----------|-------------------|-------|
| Per-test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | `TestContext` | Each test method |
| Per-class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | `ClassHookContext` | Once per class |
| Per-assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | `AssemblyHookContext` | Once per assembly |
| Per-session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | `TestSessionContext` | Once for entire run |

All hook methods must be **`static`** and return **`Task`** (or `ValueTask`). The `Test`, `Class`, `Assembly`, and `TestSession` identifiers come from `using static TUnit.Core.HookType;` (or qualify as `HookType.Test`, etc.).
